# Git Flow (this repo)

Follow [`docs/GIT_FLOW.md`](docs/GIT_FLOW.md). Summary:

- Long-lived: `main` (production / Vercel), `develop` (integration)
- Topic work: branch from `develop` as `feature/*`, `fix/*`, or `chore/*`
- **Always** use a pull request — no direct product pushes to `main` or `develop`
- `main` accepts **only** `release/*` and `hotfix/*`
- Merge methods:
  - Into `develop` from feature/fix/chore → **squash**
  - Into `develop` from release/hotfix → **merge commit** (never squash)
  - Into `main` from release/hotfix → **merge commit** (never squash)
- Versioning: bump app counters on merge into `develop`; finalize release
  version only on `release/*` (or `hotfix/*` for patches). See
  [`docs/VERSIONING.md`](docs/VERSIONING.md).
